Z||000000||2xsess||09-08-2000||07:00 PM||||Okay all you gurus. I need some input here please. I'm looking to buy my next Fiero,obviously I'm on a limited budget. I've found an 86Gt and an 85Gt both for the same price. They're both 4spds,w/sunroof,A/C,subwoofer,p/w,p/l.The 86 needs a serious buff job and the front facia repainted,and an A/C line. The 85 only needs slight touchups. I'm going to look at them tomorrow. I had an 86Gt and I didn't think it handled as good as my 84 and 85 4cyls. I've never had an notchback v6 so I need input.<BR>Thank you all!!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Coconut||09-08-2000||07:28 PM||||I'd go for the '85 (in my humble opinion)solely on the fact that there aren't as many GT notchbacks out there as there are GT fastbacks. I used to have an '86 SE but traded it for my fastback. I LOVE the profile of the fastback, but sure do miss having the notchback.<P>Cruisin'On,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||stimpy||09-08-2000||07:38 PM||||Really just depends on your priorities.  The 85 does sound like the better deal, and although I own an 86, I do think notchback V6 Fieros are very cool. I think it's best to go with the one in the best condition unless you have to have a fastback!<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
